sn12.64:4.1 | S: Suppose an artist or painter had some dye, red lac, turmeric, indigo, or rose madder. And on a polished plank or a wall or a canvas they’d create the form of a woman or a man, whole in its major and minor limbs. | T: “Suppose, bhikkhus, an artist or a painter, using dye or lac or turmeric or indigo or crimson, would create the figure of a man or a woman complete in all its features on a well-polished plank or wall or canvas.
sn12.64:4.2 | S: In the same way, if there is desire, relishing, and craving for edible food, consciousness becomes established there and grows. | T: So too, if there is lust for the nutriment edible food,
