sn12.64:9.2 | S: If there is no desire, relishing, and craving for mental intention as fuel … | T: for the nutriment mental volition …
sn12.64:9.3 | S: If there is no desire, relishing, and craving for consciousness as fuel, consciousness doesn’t become established there and doesn’t grow. | T: for the nutriment consciousness … consciousness does not become established there and come to growth.
sn12.64:9.4 | S: Where consciousness is not established and doesn’t grow, name and form are not conceived. | T: Where consciousness does not become established and come to growth …
sn12.64:9.5 | S: Where name and form are not conceived, there is no growth of choices. | T: (none)
sn12.64:9.6 | S: Where choices don’t grow, there is no regeneration into a new state of existence in the future. | T: (none)
sn12.64:9.7 | S: Where there is no regeneration into a new state of existence in the future, there is no rebirth, old age, and death in the future. | T: (none)
sn12.64:9.8 | S: Where there is no rebirth, old age, and death in the future, I say there’s no sorrow, anguish, and distress.” | T: … I say that is without sorrow, anguish, and despair.”
